odeficiency syndrome: recurrent infections and growth delay may suggest immune compromise, but MRI-documented structural airway dilation shifts focus toward anatomical disease", "Cystic fibrosis: could explain bronchiectasis and growth delay, but no sweat testing or genetic confirmation mentioned", "Primary ciliary dyskinesia: associated with chronic airway/sinus disease and cardiac anomalies (e.g., Kartagener syndrome), but no situs inversus or specific ciliary findings documented", "Congenital heart disease with secondary pulmonary complications: tricuspid stenosis could contribute to pulmonary hypertension, but MRI shows primary airway dilation rather than secondary vascular changes"], "alarm_features": ["Persistent 25th percentile growth since birth (potential failure to thrive)", "History of tricuspid stenosis (congenital cardiac anomaly)", "Recurrent respiratory infections with structural airway findings"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Cystic Fibrosis with Pulmonary and Sinus Manifestations", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.5767690253671562, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Primary structural airway dilation supports inherited conditions like cystic fibrosis over acquired infection-related changes."], "evidence_against": ["Lack of confirmatory testing for cystic fibrosis slightly reduces its likelihood but does not eliminate it in this clinical context."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Ciliary Dysfunction Syndrome with Sinus and Pulmonary Manifestations", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.19934333958724204, "posterior": 0.20026702269692923,